<ac:structured-macro ac:name="details"><ac:parameter ac:name="id">dbsec-platform</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><table><tbody><tr><th><p>Platform</p></th><td><p>IBM Db2</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Product</p></th><td><p>IBM Db2 for Linux, UNIX and Windows (LUW), including HADR</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Versions in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[e.g., 11.5.x]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Policy</p></th><td><p><code>SEC-POL-DB-001</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Technical basis</p></th><td><p>CIS IBM Db2 11 Benchmark</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable audit file(s)</p></th><td><p>CIS_IBM_DB2_11_*.audit (database checks) + Unix audit for instance file permissions</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable credential</p></th><td><p>Database credential, type DB2 (database name and port; one entry per database)</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Control prefix</p></th><td><p><code>DB2</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Instances in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[count or link to CMDB]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Controls</p></th><td><p>11</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Automated (Tenable)</p></th><td><p>7 of 11</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Compliance % (last scan)</p></th><td><p>0%</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Open CRITICAL / HIGH</p></th><td><p>0</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Last Tenable scan</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Owner team</p></th><td><p><em>[Team]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Next review due</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr></tbody></table></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Company policy – SEC-POL-DB-001</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p>This page is part of the company Database Security Configuration Policy (SEC-POL-DB-001). Its requirements are mandatory for every database in scope. Deviations need an approved entry in the DB Security – Exceptions Register. CIS Benchmarks and Tenable audit files are the technical basis and assessment method; where this policy differs from CIS, this policy applies.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="toc"><ac:parameter ac:name="maxLevel">2</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>
<h2>Scope &amp; applicability</h2>
<ul><li>Instance (DBM CFG) controls apply once per instance; database (DB CFG) controls apply to every database in the instance.</li><li>Db2 for z/OS and Db2 for i are out of scope of this page.</li></ul>
<h2>Tenable assessment setup</h2>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Item</p></th><th><p>Value</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan template</strong></p></td><td><p>Policy Compliance Auditing (credentialed)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Audit file(s)</strong></p></td><td><p>CIS_IBM_DB2_11_*.audit (database checks) + Unix audit for instance file permissions</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Credential</strong></p></td><td><p>Database credential, type DB2 (database name and port; one entry per database)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan account privileges</strong></p></td><td><p><code>CONNECT</code> on each database, <code>SELECT</code> on <code>SYSCAT</code> views, SYSMON authority; no SYSADM / DBADM</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Tailoring</strong></p></td><td><p>Company values from the register below override CIS defaults in the tailored audit file. Store it in <em>[repository / Tenable policy name]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Control register</h2>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">How to maintain this register</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><ul><li>One row per control. Control IDs are never renumbered or reused.</li><li><strong>Tenable Check</strong> describes what the audit item reads and its pass condition. Copy the CIS section from the audit item's <code>reference</code> field into <strong>CIS Reference</strong>.</li><li>Changing a Compliant Value is a policy change: record it in the change log and get approval.</li><li>After every scan, update Compliance % and Open CRITICAL / HIGH in the table at the top of the page.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Control ID</p></th><th><p>Control Name</p></th><th><p>Domain</p></th><th><p>Requirement</p></th><th><p>Severity</p></th><th><p>Compliant Value</p></th><th><p>Tenable Check (Audit / Query)</p></th><th><p>CIS Reference</p></th><th><p>Assessment</p></th><th><p>Last Review (Date / By)</p></th><th><p>Comments</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-VER-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Supported release with current fix pack</p></td><td><p><code>VER</code></p></td><td><p>The instance runs a supported Db2 release at the latest mod pack / fix pack within the patch SLA.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>db2level</code> in the approved version list</p></td><td><p><code>SELECT * FROM SYSIBMADM.ENV_INST_INFO</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-AAA-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Server-side authentication</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>The instance authenticates users on the server with encrypted credentials and does not trust client authentication.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>AUTHENTICATION = SERVER_ENCRYPT</code> (or KERBEROS / GSSPLUGIN); <code>TRUST_ALLCLNTS = NO</code>; <code>TRUST_CLNTAUTH = SERVER</code></p></td><td><p>Query <code>SYSIBMADM.DBMCFG</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-AAA-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Dedicated authority groups</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>SYSADM, SYSCTRL, SYSMAINT and SYSMON authorities map to dedicated OS groups with approved members.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>SYSADM_GROUP</code>, <code>SYSCTRL_GROUP</code>, <code>SYSMAINT_GROUP</code>, <code>SYSMON_GROUP</code> set to dedicated groups</p></td><td><p>Query <code>SYSIBMADM.DBMCFG</code>; group membership via Unix audit</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-PRIV-001</strong></p></td><td><p>PUBLIC privileges revoked</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>PUBLIC holds no database authorities; databases are created RESTRICTIVE or the defaults are revoked.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>No <code>CONNECTAUTH</code>, <code>CREATETABAUTH</code>, <code>BINDADDAUTH</code>, <code>IMPLSCHEMAAUTH</code> for PUBLIC in <code>SYSCAT.DBAUTH</code></p></td><td><p>Query <code>SYSCAT.DBAUTH WHERE GRANTEE = 'PUBLIC'</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-PRIV-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Separation of duties for SECADM</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>SECADM is held by a security administrator who does not hold DBADM or DATAACCESS.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>No grantee holds SECADM together with DBADM or DATAACCESS</p></td><td><p>Query <code>SYSCAT.DBAUTH</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-PRIV-003</strong></p></td><td><p>Catalog access restricted</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>SELECT on the system catalog is not granted to PUBLIC where applications do not need it.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>No PUBLIC SELECT on <code>SYSCAT.*</code> / <code>SYSIBM.*</code> (RESTRICT_ACCESS = YES)</p></td><td><p>Query <code>SYSCAT.TABAUTH</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-CRYPTO-001</strong></p></td><td><p>TLS-only communication</p></td><td><p><code>CRYPTO</code></p></td><td><p>Clients connect over TLS 1.2 or higher; plaintext TCP/IP is disabled.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>DB2COMM = SSL</code>; <code>SSL_VERSIONS = TLSV12,TLSV13</code>; <code>SSL_SVR_KEYDB</code> set</p></td><td><p>Query <code>SYSIBMADM.DBMCFG</code>; <code>db2set -all</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-CRYPTO-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Native encryption at rest</p></td><td><p><code>CRYPTO</code></p></td><td><p>Databases classified Confidential or higher use Db2 native encryption with a keystore (PKCS#12 or KMIP).</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>ENCRYPTED = YES</code> in <code>SYSPROC.ADMIN_GET_ENCRYPTION_INFO</code></p></td><td><p><code>SELECT * FROM TABLE(SYSPROC.ADMIN_GET_ENCRYPTION_INFO())</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Data classification comes from the CMDB.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-LOG-001</strong></p></td><td><p>db2audit configured</p></td><td><p><code>LOG</code></p></td><td><p>The instance audit facility records security-relevant categories and is archived to the SIEM.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>AUDIT</code>, <code>CHECKING</code>, <code>OBJMAINT</code>, <code>SECMAINT</code>, <code>SYSADMIN</code>, <code>VALIDATE</code> = BOTH; database audit policy assigned</p></td><td><p><code>db2audit describe</code> via Unix audit; <code>SYSCAT.AUDITPOLICIES</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-NET-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Discovery disabled</p></td><td><p><code>NET</code></p></td><td><p>The instance and databases cannot be discovered by DB2 discovery requests.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>DISCOVER = DISABLE</code>; <code>DISCOVER_INST = DISABLE</code>; <code>DISCOVER_DB = DISABLE</code></p></td><td><p>Query <code>SYSIBMADM.DBMCFG</code> / <code>SYSIBMADM.DBCFG</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>DB2-OS-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Instance owner and file permissions</p></td><td><p><code>OS</code></p></td><td><p>The instance runs under a dedicated non-root owner; the instance home and sqllib directories are not writable by others.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Instance owner ≠ root; <code>sqllib</code> and database paths mode 750 or stricter</p></td><td><p>Unix audit: file permission checks</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><em>[DB2-DOMAIN-NNN]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Short control name]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Domain]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[What must be true]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Value that passes]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Audit item / query + pass condition]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS §]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[AUTOMATED / PARTIAL / MANUAL / PLANNED / NOT FEASIBLE]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Caveats, exception IDs]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Control details</h2>
<p>Optional. Copy this expand for each control that needs more detail than the register holds.</p>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="expand"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">DB2-VER-001 – Supported release with current fix pack – details (example)</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><table><tbody><tr><th><p>Field</p></th><th><p>Value</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Applies to</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[All instances / production only / CDB only / ...]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Rationale / risk</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Why the control exists; what happens if it is not met]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Tenable audit item</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Description string of the check in the .audit file]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Audit file and version</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[File name, version, date]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Check type</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[SQL query / config file / registry / manual]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Pass condition</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Exact condition]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Not applicable when</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[e.g., feature not installed or not licensed]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Remediation impact</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[None / restart required / application change]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>CIS reference</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Benchmark name, version, section]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Exceptions</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[EXC-IDs, or None]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><strong>Evidence query (example, verify before use):</strong></p>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code"><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[SELECT NAME, VALUE FROM SYSIBMADM.DBMCFG
 WHERE NAME IN ('authentication', 'trust_allclnts', 'trust_clntauth', 'discover');]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<p><strong>Remediation (example, apply through change management):</strong></p>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code"><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[db2 update dbm cfg using AUTHENTICATION SERVER_ENCRYPT TRUST_ALLCLNTS NO TRUST_CLNTAUTH SERVER
db2stop
db2start]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
